 convenience store  it won the akutagawa prize and it sold  millions of copies and it was adapted as  a radio drama  the author murata sayaka clearly struck  a nerve as one reader tweeted what is  normal anyway and why should people who  aren't normal have to suffer  now to judge by literary prizes and  movie adaptations japan is full of  people finding meaning beyond  traditional families there are widows on  quests of self-discovery there are  secretive bitcoin miners  but it's hard for traditionalists to  embrace that future  it requires giving up the idea of  japanese empire 1.0 japan's military  empire in the early 20th century  and also empire 2.0  japan has an economic superpower in the  second half of the 20th century  and forsaking those visions of empire  accepting japan as a slower growth solo  society that requires a new vision of  japan  and depending on one's perspective that  new vision of japan it's either  exhilarating or terrifying  [Music]  you

